-- title:
--   Slot identities for G₁₅ under the icosahedral half-turn, part 1
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero and let $\alpha,\beta,s\in K$ satisfy the four relations $\alpha\beta=-s$, $2\alpha^{2}=-5-s$, $2\beta^{2}=s-5$ and $s^{2}=5$. The conclusion is a conjunction of ten polynomial identities in $\alpha$ and $\beta$ alone (the auxiliary element $s$ occurs only in the hypotheses). Each left-hand side is a $\mathbb{Z}$-linear combination, with between four and sixteen terms and explicit integer coefficients, of monomials $\alpha^{a}\beta^{b}$ with $a+b=19$; thus each is homogeneous of degree $19$. Six of the ten identities assert that the corresponding combination vanishes, namely the second, third, fourth, seventh, eighth and ninth conjuncts. The remaining four assert equalities with a linear right-hand side: the first equals $5^{9}\,\alpha=1953125\,\alpha$, the fifth equals $57\cdot 5^{9}\,\beta=111328125\,\beta$, the sixth equals $171\cdot 5^{9}\,\alpha=333984375\,\alpha$, and the tenth equals $247\cdot 5^{9}\,\beta=482421875\,\beta$. The coefficients are as written in the statement; no further structure is asserted.
--
--   These are the coefficient certificates, in ten of the relevant slots, for the behaviour of the numerator $G_{15}(u)=57u^{15}-247u^{10}-171u^{5}-1$ of the Rubin–Silverberg Möbius datum under Klein's icosahedral half-turn $U=s^{-1}\begin{pmatrix}-\alpha&\beta\\ \beta&\alpha\end{pmatrix}$, where $\alpha=\zeta-\zeta^{4}$, $\beta=\zeta^{2}-\zeta^{3}$, $s=\sqrt5$ for a primitive fifth root of unity $\zeta$; stating them over an arbitrary field of characteristic zero in terms of abstract $\alpha,\beta,s$ subject to the four listed relations turns them into a finite polynomial certificate. They are used by [`RubinSilverberg.icoU_datumG`](thm.html#RubinSilverberg.icoU_datumG), the equivariance of the datum numerator under $U$.
-- source:
